      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: BANK – CONCEPT, ROLE AND NEED"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Commercial banks operate primarily to accept deposits from the public and advance loans to borrowers.",
        "Secondary functions of commercial banks are divided into Agency Functions (acting on behalf of customers) and Utility Functions (general services like lockers).",
        "Credit creation is the process by which commercial banks create derivative deposits based on initial cash reserves.",
        "Bank nationalisation was executed in two major waves (1969 and 1980) to realign credit priorities toward agriculture and social sector development.",
        "Regional Rural Banks (RRBs) and Cooperative Banks serve targeted regional and agricultural financial requirements."
      ],
      "id": "m3d56yy"
