    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "14 major commercial banks were nationalised on 19 July 1969 with deposits over Rs 50 crore; 6 more were nationalised in 1980 with deposits over Rs 200 crore.",
        "Regional Rural Banks (RRBs) were set up under the RRB Act, 1976 following the Narasimham Working Group recommendations of 1975.",
        "Distinction between Agency Functions (cheque collection, payment execution) and Utility Functions (issuing foreign exchange, safe custody lockers) is frequently asked in SSC exams."
      ],
